Enable Explicit Resource Management by default in the Kandelo shell.

ESR 140 ships the Explicit Resource Management implementation (`using` /
`await using`) behind the compile-time macro
ENABLE_EXPLICIT_RESOURCE_MANAGEMENT, which the Kandelo mozconfig now turns
on with `--enable-explicit-resource-management`. The frontend still gates the
`using` keyword on the runtime pref
`javascript.options.experimental.explicit_resource_management`, which the
StaticPrefList defaults to `false` on the ESR (non-Nightly) channel. Because
node.wasm is invoked as `node <script>` and never receives the shell's
`--enable-explicit-resource-management` CLI flag, that default left the parser
rejecting `using`.

node.wasm targets modern Node semantics, where Explicit Resource Management is
enabled by default. Turn the engine pref on by default here so the frontend
parses `using`. An explicit `--disable-explicit-resource-management` still wins
because it is applied afterward.

--- a/js/src/shell/js.cpp
+++ b/js/src/shell/js.cpp
@@ -13053,6 +13053,11 @@
   }
 #endif
 #ifdef ENABLE_EXPLICIT_RESOURCE_MANAGEMENT
+  // Kandelo: node.wasm targets modern Node semantics where Explicit Resource
+  // Management (`using`/`await using`) is enabled by default. Turn the engine
+  // pref on so the frontend parses `using`; an explicit
+  // --disable-explicit-resource-management below still overrides this.
+  JS::Prefs::set_experimental_explicit_resource_management(true);
   if (op.getBoolOption("enable-explicit-resource-management")) {
     JS::Prefs::set_experimental_explicit_resource_management(true);
   }
